[I] A library that exposes a event API on top of Linux futexes

[T] libxshmfence offers a CPU-based synchronization primitive compatible
[T] with X SyncFence objects that can be shared between processes via file
[T] descriptor passing. On Linux it is implemented with futexes, elsewhere
[T] with POSIX mutexes and condition variables; it is used by DRI3 and Mesa.

[U] https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/xorg/lib/libxshmfence

[A] X.org Foundation {http://www.X.org}
[M] Gerardo Di Iorio <arete74@gmail.com>

[C] base/x11
[F] CROSS

[L] OpenSource
[V] 1.3.3
